"""Live-answers probe set — 81 questions from "Regenold — Questions & Live Answers" (2026-08).

Each row carries the file's question, its live answer as gold_answer, and the file's References as expected_refs (HEAD-projected per the R337 corpus invariant). A small set of gold corrections is applied where the source file's own references are provably wrong for the question (verified against the Act's provision text):

* Q5  - Article 49 (registration) dropped; Article 13 is the transparency duty.
* Q6  - the file's ref (Article 108, sectoral amendments) is a cached mis-answer;
        scope is Article 2, 'AI system' Article 3(1), GPAI Article 3(63)/51. The
        gold answer is rewritten accordingly.
* Q11 - Article 52 (GPAI systemic-risk notification) dropped; testing/validation
        data governance is Article 10.
* Q27 - Article 50.1 (interaction transparency) dropped; election influence is
        Annex III(8)(a) via Article 6(2).
* Q29 - Article 46 (exceptional-placing derogation) dropped; emergency triage is
        Annex III(5)(d) via Article 6(2).
* Q42 - the file's refs (48, 102, 3.11, Annex I) are flagged IN the answer as
        irrelevant; Article 26(7) is operative.
* Q77 - Article 3.25 (post-market monitoring) -> Article 3.49 (serious incident,
        as the answer itself states).
* Q55/Q56 - out-of-scope probes ((none) refs, refusal gold_answer, keyword gold)
        — they measure the OOS guard, not retrieval.

Schema matches ``_norm_single`` (probe_set): id, question, expected_refs, expected_keywords, gold_answer.
"""

